public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EtaSheafReductionDerivedIso
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.IdealGeneratedByNonzerodivisor

import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Tag 0GT9 in Situation 0GT4: the canonical isomorphism, unconditionally

Situation 20.55.2 (Tag 0GT4) is a ringed space `(X, O_X)` together with an ideal sheaf
`I ⊂ O_X` satisfying **condition (1) of Tag 0GT3**: locally the ideal is generated by a section
which is a nonzerodivisor.  Tag 0GT9 asserts, in that situation, a canonical isomorphism

`Lη_I M ⊗^L O_X/I ⟶ H^•(M/I)`

in `D(O_X)`.  `EtaSheafReductionDerivedIso.lean` built that arrow and the isomorphism as data,
but conditionally: on `Reduction.HasStalkBocksteinSquare`, the stalkwise comparison square which
is the source's last sentence.  `EtaSheafBocksteinStalk.lean` now proves that square
(`Reduction.map_reductionComparison_comp_bocksteinChainStalkTermIso`), and this file discharges
the remaining datum of the predicate — a generator of the stalk ideal — from the situation's own
hypothesis, making the isomorphism unconditional.

## Main definitions

* `reductionComparisonQIsoOfRegular`: **the canonical isomorphism of Tag 0GT9 in `D(O_X)`, in
  Situation 0GT4, with no hypothesis beyond the situation.**  Its forward map is the canonical
  arrow `reductionComparisonQ` by `rfl` (`reductionComparisonQIsoOfRegular_hom`).

## Main results

* `exists_stalkGenerator_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`: at every point of a ringed space whose
  ideal sheaf is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor, the stalk ideal has a generator which is
  a nonzerodivisor.  **Nothing is assumed about the stalks of the structure sheaf**: the
  trivializing neighbourhood of the situation supplies the freeness of rank one directly
  (`Eta.isFiniteFreeStalkOfRank_one_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`), where condition (2) alone
  would need every stalk to be a local ring.
* `hasStalkBocksteinSquare_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular` and
  `hasStalkBocksteinSquare_of_isLocalRing`: `Reduction.HasStalkBocksteinSquare` holds — the first
  in Situation 0GT4, the second under condition (2) of Tag 0GT3 on a space with local stalks.
  These are the first inhabitants of that predicate.
* `quasiIso_reductionComparisonChainMap_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular` and
  `acyclic_reductionComparisonKernel_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`: the chain-level forms.
* `isIso_reductionComparisonQ_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`: **the canonical arrow of Tag 0GT9
  is invertible in `D(O_X)`**, in Situation 0GT4.

## Implementation notes

### Where the generator comes from, and why it is not an extra hypothesis

`Reduction.exists_stalkGenerator` produces a generator from condition (2) of Tag 0GT3 — `I`
invertible — but only on a space all of whose structure-sheaf stalks are local rings, because
over a general ringed space an invertible module need not have free stalks.  That hypothesis is
no part of Situation 0GT4.  Situation 0GT4's own hypothesis is the *stronger* condition (1), and
it gives the generator with no hypothesis on the stalks at all: a neighbourhood on which the
ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor trivializes the stalk.  So the statements below are
Tag 0GT9 in the source's own situation, with no stand-in and no added hypothesis.

The `[Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible …]` binder is kept alongside
`IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular` rather than derived by a `letI`, because the statements name
objects — `etaModIdealComplex`, `bocksteinChainComplex`, `reductionComparisonQ` — whose types
mention it.  Condition (1) implies it
(`Stacks.IdealTorsion.isInvertible_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`) and `IsInvertible` is a
`Prop`, so nothing is assumed twice.

### Which declarations carry the tag

The tag's own words are "there is a canonical isomorphism".  Two declarations state that and
both carry `@[stacks 0GT9]`: `reductionComparisonQIsoOfRegular`, which is the isomorphism as
*data* with its forward map pinned to the canonical arrow, and
`isIso_reductionComparisonQ_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`, which is the same fact as a
proposition about that arrow.  Neither has a hypothesis outside Situation 0GT4.

The derived category is taken at the standard localization model, as in
`EtaSheafReductionDerivedIso.lean`, so an importer wanting to compose with other
derived-category statements must put the same
`attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard` in scope.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT4)
